now a mega job fair is happening inside  the las vegas convention center  with the federal pandemic unemployment  benefits due to expire in two months in  september  clark county officials say now is the  time to find a job  if you're unemployed bianca holman takes  us inside more than 125  employers and more than 14 thousand jobs  this job fair  is getting folks back to work it's  amazing because i've been in town for 15  years and i've never  even during the downturn it was never an  issue with employment  but as you can see i mean a lot of  employers here looking for people  qualified people locally owned gen 3  hospitality company along with  government agencies  and medical companies need help five  thousand job seekers were able to access  laptops and printers for free resume  checks and employment  and training help all at no cost people  had interviews on the spot and in some  cases  job offers ensuring no lapse in  household income for many when extra  federal  unemployment benefits expire leaders say  this event will benefit families across  the valley  this is something that has taken an  enormous effort to get it organized  and it is paid off i mean here we are  and we're pulling off something that's  never been done before  the fact that we are providing this  service and to see people coming back  out a lot of people are still a little  bit leery about getting out in the world  so the fact that this many people came  out is a very positive sign  and the southern nevada health district  even offered free coven 19 vaccinations  reporting from the las vegas convention  center bianca holman 8 news now
 

